# NSQ-gate reach on INTER frames, per grid cell (§1z³⁵)
#
# commit:  ed2f655a (the fixed tree)      host: aarch64-apple-darwin
# tool:    tools/nsq_inter_reach_census.sh, run serially after the gate chain
#          (an earlier overlapping run mis-reported one cell; see
#          docs/WORKING-ON-THIS.md §5)
# axes:    this file  = the 96-cell grid, frames=2, shift 3
#          the -p5 file = {uniform,gradient,diag,screen} x {64,128} x
#                        {q20,q40,q55} x {p5,p6,p8}, frames=2, shift 3
# columns: SPENTRY shapes entering skip_processing_nsq on frame 1; SKIP1..4
#          killed by gate 1 (split rate) / 2 (sq txs) / 3 (recon dist) / 4
#          (shapes); RDENTRY entries into skip_by_recon_dist; RECONDIST past
#          its early-outs (the parent-mode read); MODEDIFF of those, parent
#          is inter (ymode != block_mi.mode)
# totals:  grid: SPENTRY 304 (p6 248 / p8 56), SKIP1 302, RDENTRY 2,
#          RECONDIST 2, MODEDIFF 2 -- both on gradient 16x16 q20 p6
#          p5 file: SPENTRY 584, SKIP1 584, RDENTRY 0
